{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370797-sorcerous-initiation-the-wyld-huntsmen","id":1370797,"title":"Sorcerous Initiation: The Wyld Huntsmen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-27T11:11:35-08:00","id":1370797,"title":"Sorcerous Initiation: The Wyld Huntsmen","content":"More than once, in more than one game, people have wanted to play Witchers.<br /> <br /> Exalted is no exception, and there's been much, <i>much</i> dissent as to what even works. Some would say they could be a type of exigent (I like this one). Some would say they are a type of thaumaturge (ehh...). Some would say sorcery alone covers this (maybe?).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Kx-JAJ90FygAWjPo0OPaWJals5hLQdqVFDO_lLgjMPI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">So eventually I just decided to add everything together to the best of my ability.</a><br /> <br /> The focus here is in the &quot;gish-like magically empowered fighter outcast&quot; vibes the witchers universally have. I drew liberally from Soul-Perfecting Elixir and Talisman of 10k Eyes, as they already play into some aspects of this type of character, and added sign magic as both a sorcerous initiation and a set of thaumaturgical rituals.<br /> <br /> I translated the setting's signs as thaumaturgy, exploring what I think would be the highest ends such rituals could attain in combat. They, along with all of the Shaping Rituals, are designed to play well in combat.<br /> <br /> I hope someone enjoys this one, and if you have any ideas, especially on balance, please let me know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T06:40:17-08:00","id":1373370,"title":"","content":"This is amazing. I am stealing this for my campaign. Might add some traps, potions, bombs and other witcher things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T13:43:51-08:00","id":1373430,"title":"","content":"Oiled Blade and Sprung Trap requires Joining Battle with a stratagem applied, right? But I thought stratagems only work in strategic warfare -- i.e., when at least one side brought an army.<br /> <br /> I feel like a Wyld Huntperson should have some way to prep the battlefield even against a small number of opponents. That's what they'd do if they thought they needed the edge, right?<br /> <br /> Is it expected that all Wyld Huntsmen are Exalted? It seems like it would get expensive for a mortal to use this initiation, since it essentially requires thaumaturgy. As I understand it, all Exalted sorcerers get access to thaumaturgy free, but mortal sorcerers do not. So a mortal Wyld Huntsperson would need to be born a thaumaturge <i>and</i> manage to learn sorcery.<br /> <br /> I ask in part because &quot;let's mutate these dudes to give them an edge against the Anathema&quot; seems like something the DBs would much rather do to mortal henchmen and not themselves.<br /> <br /> TBH, I think the closest proper analogue to Witchers in Exalted would be something like the Legion of Silence, who are warped through some crazy blend of sorcery during their training. When we get the Exigents book, it might be interesting to see if those rules could be used to build Witcher-equivalents as a unique and powerful type of God-Blooded, perhaps sired by the God of Monster-Slaying or something. (The issue with actual Exigents is that they're generally unique.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T17:20:03-08:00","id":1373461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370797-sorcerous-initiation-the-wyld-huntsmen?p=1373430#post1373430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oiled Blade and Sprung Trap requires Joining Battle with a stratagem applied, right? But I thought stratagems only work in strategic warfare -- i.e., when at least one side brought an army.<br /> <br /> I feel like a Wyld Huntperson should have some way to prep the battlefield even against a small number of opponents. That's what they'd do if they thought they needed the edge, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are mostly correct, but not wholly. The Stratagem system is <i>intended</i> for battle groups.<br /> <br /> That said, there's nothing keeping you from enjoying it without them, and it adds an interesting layer of depth to the scene that makes sense for ambush fighters of any sort - and few are as prone to try that as the Wyld Huntsmen and Huntresses.<br /> <br /> The basic problem that springs up - how to roll stratagems when there isn't a commander on the opposide side - happens with or without battlegroups. The solution is to either go uncontested (for a completely unprepared and unwary enemy) or substitute a awareness roll just to resist it. Most monsters would thus have a chance to spot the trap and avoid it (and the clever ones might even spring their own).<br /> <br /> The second problem - what stratagems make sense - is basically the norm: Only stratagems that make sense are usable in the first place, regardless of composition.<br /> You will not force a Back to the Sea on a mutated fogshark fighting on an open field! But if you lure it to the right place and collapse part of the exit, or fight it in its breeding grounds...<br /> Likewise, &quot;ambush&quot; doesn't mean much when we already have standard surprise penalties for individuals - so you use those instead.<br /> <br /> The most common form this will take in gameplay is in shaping how the PCs will cooperate. Something like Pincer Attack needs only that you have multiple characters on your side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it expected that all Wyld Huntsmen are Exalted? It seems like it would get expensive for a mortal to use this initiation, since it essentially requires thaumaturgy. As I understand it, all Exalted sorcerers get access to thaumaturgy free, but mortal sorcerers do not. So a mortal Wyld Huntsperson would need to be born a thaumaturge <i>and</i> manage to learn sorcery.<br /> I ask in part because &quot;let's mutate these dudes to give them an edge against the Anathema&quot; seems like something the DBs would much rather do to mortal henchmen and not themselves. </div> </div> </div>This initiation was born precisely as you say: as an attempt to give the unexalted an edge against the various Anathemas of Creation, helping the little guy while freeing up exalted resources.<br /> <br /> To represent this, this initiation gives the Wyld Huntsmen the two merits exalted sorcerers already get for free: Exalted Healing and Thaumaturge.<br /> With player characters we have the concerns of XP to regulate just how mutated they get, but NPCs don't have that. Most should approach somewhat the complete twinkery mutations allow, especially those that live to whatever &quot;old age&quot; means for such madmen.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> TBH, I think the closest proper analogue to Witchers in Exalted would be something like the Legion of Silence, who are warped through some crazy blend of sorcery during their training. When we get the Exigents book, it might be interesting to see if those rules could be used to build Witcher-equivalents as a unique and powerful type of God-Blooded, perhaps sired by the God of Monster-Slaying or something. (The issue with actual Exigents is that they're generally unique.) </div> </div> </div>I agree. This initiation is but one approach to this type of monster hunter, one accessible to every type of playable character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 03-07-2020, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T19:25:04-08:00","id":1373472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1370797-sorcerous-initiation-the-wyld-huntsmen?p=1373461#post1373461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are mostly correct, but not wholly. The Stratagem system is <i>intended</i> for battle groups.<br /> <br /> That said, there's nothing keeping you from enjoying it without them, and it adds an interesting layer of depth to the scene that makes sense for ambush fighters of any sort - and few are as prone to try that as the Wyld Huntsmen and Huntresses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking about the bit where the corebook (p. 211) says this?<br /> <br /> &quot;What follows is a simple system for strategic conflict for use whenever a battle between two military forces is imminent. This is intended to shape the clash of armies\u2014it\u2019s not intended to be used by a Circle of Solars preparing to fight a Circle of Abyssals, or for any similarly small-numbers conflicts.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure &quot;not intended&quot; is meant to be read as forbidding you to do it. If you <i>could</i> use the system in any fight ever, there would be no point in saying something like &quot;this is meant for military battles, not your scrap with a few rivals.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it would be very cool if there were a similar system for preparing the ground against an enemy, though. (I suspect it would tend to use Craft, Stealth, and/or Survival rather than War.) In fact, I think &quot;setting up tricks and traps for one or a few enemies&quot; probably has a lot <i>more</i> nifty possibilities than &quot;planning strategy against the other army&quot; (and a thaumaturge with the right tricks would have more options than most). Hell, we could start a topic about this if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11237,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","user":"Jefepato","date":". 03-07-2020, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}